    "result": "I implemented `invoice_totals` in `solution.py`, keeping the given signature, and changed no other file. Region and credit are checked first, then each line is checked for category, `qty`, `unit_price` and `discount_pct`, and any failure raises `ValueError`. Each line's net is its price times quantity, reduced by its own discount, then the 5% bulk discount is applied multiplicatively to standard lines with `qty` of 10 or more, then rounded to cents with `ROUND_HALF_UP`. Tax is the rounded net times the rate, also rounded per line. Totals are summed from the rounded line values, and `credit_used`, `total_due` and `credit_left` follow rule 6. `tax_by_rate` is keyed by integer rate, including zero-rate lines. I did not run anything, as instructed. One point to check: for an empty `lines` list, `credit_left` comes out as the full `credit` under rule 6, while the spec's \"all zeros\" could be read to include it.",
